  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&rArr;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Hence, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> at all pressures.<br />This means, repulsive tendencies will be dominant when interatomic distance are small. This means, interatomic potential is never negative but becomes positive at small interatomic distances."
